{
  "_notes": [
    "Derived from native NVRAM offsets.",
    "This map focuses on current/last game score extraction.",
    "Verify score encoding/scale with real NVRAM before production use.",
    "Player score fields currently mirror top saved score slots until per-player RAM offsets are mapped."
  ],
  "_fileformat": 0.7,
  "_metadata": {
    "version": 2,
    "platform": "capcom",
    "roms": [
      "bsb105"
    ]
  },
  "game_state": {
    "game_over": {
      "_notes": [
        "Game-in-progress flag in DRAM (volatile RAM, not in the .nv). Found via libpinmame, verified across Breakshot/Big Bang Bar/Pinball Magic: 0x000012F2 bit 0x40 is SET during a game, CLEAR in attract and at game over. invert=true so the field reads true when the game is over."
      ],
      "label": "Game Over",
      "start": "0x000012F2",
      "encoding": "bool",
      "mask": "0x40",
      "invert": true
    },
    "_notes": [
      "scores was removed: all four player entries aliased the NVRAM high-score mirror at 0x300000F0, so they reported leaderboard values instead of the game being played. Capcom keeps live scores in volatile DRAM (verified for bbb109 Player 1 at 0x00061F32); each game needs its own verified address before scores can be reinstated."
    ]
  },
